WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.304
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.304 --> 00:00:02.910
(explosions resound)

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.460
- [Reporter] These are cluster munitions,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.180
a type of weapon that the
US plans to send to Ukraine.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.040
The controversial bombs are prohibited

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.110
by multiple countries, but they are part

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:17.160
of an $800 million aid package
the Biden administration says

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.264
will strengthen Ukraine's
offensive against Russian forces.

00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:21.120
(blast pounds)

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.730
- Russia has already
spread tens of millions

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.270
of these bomblets across
Ukrainian territory.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.140
- [Reporter] Here's a breakdown

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.530
of how the cluster munition
works and why the United States

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.713
plans on sending them despite
humanitarian concerns.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.320
US cluster munitions,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.680
also known as dual-purpose
improved conventional munition,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.350
are a type of weapon that
spreads small bomblets

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.850
over a wide area.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.680
- What DPICMs bring to a
battlefield is anti-armor

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.470
and anti-personnel capability.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.210
- [Reporter] A common
type of cluster munition

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.830
is fired in artillery shells,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.980
which is what the US is
expected to give Ukraine.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.230
They can also be in the form of rockets

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.700
or dropped from a plane.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.980
The weapon opens midair to release tens

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.270
or hundreds of smaller explosive
munitions or submunitions.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.730
These submunitions can
be loaded with charges

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.110
that can penetrate armor

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.810
or munitions that can strike
multiple human targets

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:19.050
across an area as large as
several football fields.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.570
- Clearly, a capability
that would be useful

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.270
in any type of offensive operations.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.850
- [Reporter] In Ukraine,
Russia has used these munitions

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.250
as far back as the first
days of the invasion

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.020
according to Human Rights Watch.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.660
The group said one attack
struck residential areas

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.701
in Kharkiv, killing at
least three civilians.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.610
(explosions pounding)

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:43.380
Specifically, they say Russia
has used 9M55K Smerch rockets.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.660
Those are composed of
submunition containers

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.640
that have a tail fin and a fuse

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.530
and sit at the front of the rocket.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:51.000
The submunitions are designed

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.340
to attack both people and equipment.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.410
Behind those is the propellant.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.880
After the rocket is launched,

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.950
the container ejects the submunitions,

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.380
commonly by combining an explosive charge

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.850
and a spin mechanism.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.280
When the fuse of each
sub munition is triggered

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.280
on the ground or in the air, it explodes,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.370
but some of them can
also fail to detonate.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.050
These are referred to as duds,

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.420
a common issue with cluster munitions.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.360
Duds can cause long-term
hazards as they may detonate

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.480
after conflicts end and harm civilians.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.330
Human rights groups say
the first significant use

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.920
of cluster weapons was by German

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.380
and Soviet forces in World War II.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.420
The munitions released by German planes

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.400
were commonly called butterfly bombs

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.590
with an attack on the
British port of Grimsby

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.807
killing almost as many people
after the raid as during it.

00:02:37.807 --> 00:02:39.360
- [Newsreel Announcer]
This bomb may go off

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.910
as soon as it's even likely touched.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.770
It may also go off by itself

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.970
up to half an hour after it's landed.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.220
(explosion pops)

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.890
- [Reporter] The US made
extensive use of cluster munitions

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.360
during the Vietnam War,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.670
also dropping them in neighboring Laos.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.090
And since then, unexploded
bombs dropped by American planes

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.480
have killed or maimed
thousands of Laotians.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.550
More recently during the war in Iraq,

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.250
the US showered more
than 1 million bomblets

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.920
during a three-week
period of major combat.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.830
Since 2008, more than 110 countries

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.890
have signed an international
convention on cluster munitions

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.650
that prohibits all use,
transfer, production,

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.660
and stockpiling of cluster bombs.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.360
Russia and Ukraine have
not signed the agreement,

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.120
and the US is among several
other NATO countries

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.220
that are also not signatories.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.740
- The DPICM ammunition we
are delivering to Ukraine

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:33.740
will consist only of those with
a dud rate less than 2.35%.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.100
Compare that to Russia,

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.890
which has been using cluster
munitions across Ukraine

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.760
with dud rates of between 30 and 40%.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.800
- [Reporter] Cluster munitions
are already being used

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.870
by both sides in the war in Ukraine.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.170
- The difference is that Russia
is using cluster munition

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.170
to attack, to invade Ukraine.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.630
Ukraine is using cluster munition

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.540
to protect itself against an aggressor.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.010
- [Reporter] According
to Human Rights Watch,

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.830
Ukraine inherited a stockpile
of cluster munitions

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.990
after the breakup of the Soviet Union,

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.790
and the Biden administration decided

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:09.030
to provide US cluster munitions
after written assurances

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.180
that the weapons wouldn't
be used in civilian areas.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.660
- Even allies who were signatories
to the Oslo Convention,

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.960
while they cannot
formally support something

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.390
that they've signed up
to a convention against,

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.600
have indicated both privately
and many of them publicly

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.300
over the course of today that
they understand our decision.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.400
- [Reporter] The Pentagon
says the cluster munitions

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.870
could be effective when used

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.810
against Russian armored
formations and trench lines,

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.150
and US officials have
defended the decision

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.240
to supply the weapons as
necessary to prevent Ukraine

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.310
from running low on artillery ammunition

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.440
at a critical stage in the conflict.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.800
- By providing Ukraine with
DPICM artillery ammunition,

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.720
we will ensure that the Ukrainian military

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.547
has sufficient artillery
ammunition for many months to come.

00:04:52.547 --> 00:04:55.297
(dramatic music)

